# Camera Obscura capability: vulkan-1.3 (ARCHITECTURE.md §4).
# Active = present, inactive = absent. Never "failed".
# udev (70-obscura-cap-vulkan-1.3.rules) starts obscura-cap-vulkan-1.3-probe@<renderDN>.service
# per render node. Each probe is Before= and Upholds= this target, so every start of a probe
# also queues a start of this target, which runs only after the probe has decided.
#
# The condition below is the gate. Only an accepting probe writes
# /run/obscura-cap/vulkan-1.3/<renderDN>/accepted (its RuntimeDirectory=, removed when the
# probe stops or is skipped). A start of this target while no probe has accepted fails the
# condition: the target never enters "active", not even for an instant. Upholds= alone
# isn't enough: it pulls the target in like Wants= as soon as a probe starts (task 0.2b,
# VM pass of 2026-11-23). The marker is read only by this condition; capd never reads it.
#
# When the last accepting probe stops (its GPU went away; BindsTo= on the device), nothing
# upholds this target and StopWhenUnneeded stops it, without a reboot. Manual start and
# stop are refused so the state can't be faked. Units that belong to this capability use
# PartOf= and WantedBy= this target and must never Requires= or Wants= it.
[Unit]
Description=Obscura capability: Hardware-accelerated Vulkan 1.3 on an integrated or discrete GPU
Documentation=file:/usr/share/obscura/capabilities.d/vulkan-1.3.toml
StopWhenUnneeded=yes
RefuseManualStart=yes
RefuseManualStop=yes
ConditionPathExistsGlob=/run/obscura-cap/vulkan-1.3/*/accepted
